title One tool call through the pipeline

reply  "Model reply"
pre    "pre-execute listeners"
ask    "Approval"
guards "Guards"
wrap   "tools/execute wrapper"
body   "Tool body"
post   "post-execute listeners"
log    "Session record"

push, rm at reply

# Two calls from one reply pass the same stages in the same order.
pause "One reply asks for bash rm -rf build and bash git push."

# A deletion is denied, so its body never runs.
rm -> pre : blocked "A policy listener returns deny."
rm -> post "A denied call skips the body, but its error result still passes post-execute."
rm -> log : failed "The model will read: Error: rm -rf is not allowed here."

# git push needs a person's answer before it can run.
push -> pre : waiting "The policy listener returns ask."
push -> ask : waiting "The person answers allowed-once."
push -> guards : running "An allowed call still meets every guard."

# The body runs inside the wrapper, under a deadline.
push -> wrap : running "The timeout wrapper adds a deadline to the call's signal."
push -> body : running "The body watches that signal."
push -> wrap "The body returned before the deadline, so the wrapper keeps its result."

# The result is checked once more before the model sees it.
push -> post : running "A listener may replace the result, block it or add context."
push -> log : done "One tool/result per call, in the order the model asked."
